## Lab vs Natural: The Price Gap Is Real

Certified market data shows a consistent 40–60% price difference between lab and natural radiant cut eternity bands at equivalent grades.

That gap is not shrinking. Lab prices have continued to fall as production scales. Natural prices have held because supply is fixed.

This is not a quality difference. Lab diamonds are chemically identical to mined diamonds. They have the same hardness, the same refractive index, the same fire and brilliance. The difference is origin, not quality.

For an eternity band, the grade tradeoff is also different from a solitaire. You are not looking at one large center stone — you are looking at many small stones side by side. Each individual stone in a 3ct radiant eternity band is roughly 0.15–0.25ct. At that size, clarity and color grade differences are less visible to the naked eye than in a solitaire.

This means you can often go one color grade lower and one clarity grade lower in an eternity band versus a solitaire without any visible difference. The certified market inventory below uses H-I color and SI1-SI2 clarity for natural bands — grades that would be risky in a solitaire but are perfectly clean in small eternity stones.

