## Expert Summary

A radiant cut eternity band has two rules every buyer must follow before deciding on carat weight or metal. The No-Resize Rule means you confirm your exact ring size three times before ordering — the band cannot be altered after purchase. The Rectangle Flow Effect means you get more face-up coverage per carat than a round eternity band, which changes how carat weight should be chosen. Within the lab range, the 3ct white gold at $3,000 is the best-value pick — a jump from 2ct costs $324 for a 50% increase in band width. The 5ct at $3,876 delivers the lowest cost per carat if budget allows. For natural, the 3ct at $6,435 is the right call before price inflects hard at 4ct. For daily wear, choose the bezel setting over prong — micro-prongs on eternity bands snag and bend in ways that solitaire prongs do not. Follow The No-Resize Rule and the rest of the decisions fall into place.

